{"card_hash": "1975c508060bb6e60056409f66d3749792f428c41ae3ed6604506c91efe39280", "channel": "Vercel", "chars": 6576, "chars_all_clips": 6576, "chars_chosen_clips": 1440, "clip_count": 9, "clips": [{"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=7-zJPwJC11Q\u0026t=16s", "end": 65.31, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "97cbcae3d9665e49e32c9a1cc9e53c1a1bf21ec1fe9884ee5c093af62d84ee6d", "start": 16.03, "text": "Hey everyone. My name is Malte, I'm the CTO for Cell. Thanks for joining us today. In early January, we gave everyone in our company a mandate. Figure out how to multiply your output. And seeing what people built continues to blow us away. ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=7-zJPwJC11Q\u0026t=65s", "end": 114.91, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "e433c65651751427b6ea180b31910576479b84493d9c5efc475dd16062cf7d3f", "start": 65.31, "text": "completely different under the hood. Slack supports native streaming. You can stream tokens directly into a message as the LLM generates them. Discord, you have to post, edit, post, edit. GitHub, no streaming at all. Slack has models, Disco", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=7-zJPwJC11Q\u0026t=165s", "end": 213.949, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "3e3f333752635bfb3e55efdb2be94abe4dd7f012e1b618078b2e43343f86939c", "start": 165.63, "text": "codebase with any language. So, I started building and I sent the first version of the V0 Slack app to my friends. And the first thing they asked was, \"Can I also use this in linear issues?\" And can I tag it from a GitHub PR comment? It rem", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=7-zJPwJC11Q\u0026t=261s", "end": 311.83, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "0939154e6adfa662eeb3328ed3708bee2d7084ccb95401be8a55c7385a008846", "start": 261.229, "text": "response. Game changing, I know. And if you look at the code, you can see how easy it was for me to create this bot. All I had to do was create a new chat instance and add an on mention listener and post hello world back to the thread. That", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=7-zJPwJC11Q\u0026t=311s", "end": 362.87, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "3ea1d48ca0705f22d09b36a25d8a2cbbf85e03debbaf48c127e4b346693e8ef2", "start": 311.83, "text": "button. We're also going to add an action listener that will say the user's full name clicked continue when we click it. Back in Slack, I'm going to mention my bot again and as you can expect, we get exactly what we built. The components re", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=7-zJPwJC11Q\u0026t=409s", "end": 498.96, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "61d73e86ec6051ca5cef3a35fd6efd4e509d121ed6662fb569e1162453e37915", "start": 409.39, "text": "or Telegram? With the Chat SDK, it's easy. I add a on direct message listener and the adapter needed. Now, anyone who DMs the agent gets the same experience. If I open WhatsApp on the web and say, \"Hi, how are you doing?\" we'll see the agen", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "Uncategorized", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=7-zJPwJC11Q\u0026t=16s", "end": 65.31, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "97cbcae3d9665e49e32c9a1cc9e53c1a1bf21ec1fe9884ee5c093af62d84ee6d", "start": 16.03, "text": "Hey everyone. My name is Malte, I'm the CTO for Cell. Thanks for joining us today. In early January, we gave everyone in our company a mandate. Figure out how to multiply your output. And seeing what people built continues to blow us away. ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=7-zJPwJC11Q\u0026t=65s", "end": 114.91, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "e433c65651751427b6ea180b31910576479b84493d9c5efc475dd16062cf7d3f", "start": 65.31, "text": "completely different under the hood. Slack supports native streaming. You can stream tokens directly into a message as the LLM generates them. Discord, you have to post, edit, post, edit. GitHub, no streaming at all. Slack has models, Disco", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=7-zJPwJC11Q\u0026t=165s", "end": 213.949, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "3e3f333752635bfb3e55efdb2be94abe4dd7f012e1b618078b2e43343f86939c", "start": 165.63, "text": "codebase with any language. So, I started building and I sent the first version of the V0 Slack app to my friends. And the first thing they asked was, \"Can I also use this in linear issues?\" And can I tag it from a GitHub PR comment? It rem", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=7-zJPwJC11Q\u0026t=261s", "end": 311.83, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "0939154e6adfa662eeb3328ed3708bee2d7084ccb95401be8a55c7385a008846", "start": 261.229, "text": "response. Game changing, I know. And if you look at the code, you can see how easy it was for me to create this bot. All I had to do was create a new chat instance and add an on mention listener and post hello world back to the thread. That", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=7-zJPwJC11Q\u0026t=311s", "end": 362.87, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "3ea1d48ca0705f22d09b36a25d8a2cbbf85e03debbaf48c127e4b346693e8ef2", "start": 311.83, "text": "button. We're also going to add an action listener that will say the user's full name clicked continue when we click it. Back in Slack, I'm going to mention my bot again and as you can expect, we get exactly what we built. The components re", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=7-zJPwJC11Q\u0026t=409s", "end": 498.96, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "61d73e86ec6051ca5cef3a35fd6efd4e509d121ed6662fb569e1162453e37915", "start": 409.39, "text": "or Telegram? With the Chat SDK, it's easy. I add a on direct message listener and the adapter needed. Now, anyone who DMs the agent gets the same experience. If I open WhatsApp on the web and say, \"Hi, how are you doing?\" we'll see the agen", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "hint": null, "platform": "youtube", "profile": "librarian", "schema_version": 1, "selection_version": "spread-longest-v2", "slug": "Introducing_Chat_SDK", "source_revision": "9d1fe939792f0b57dabbf36264868308715b95aa83b29c60707e40308ae30983", "source_type": "video", "status": "evidenced", "summary_hint": null, "title": "Introducing Chat SDK", "topic": "Uncategorized", "truncated": true, "truncation": {"byte_budget": true, "fields": ["hint"], "selection": true}, "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7-zJPwJC11Q", "video_id": "7-zJPwJC11Q", "yoinked_at": "2026-05-14T23:27:45"}
